      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 19,
      "mode": 0,
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000",
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## MiniMax H3: Long Video (Context Windows)\n\n**Input Assets**\n- [sunset_boulevard_walk.png](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Comfy-Org/workflow_templates/refs/heads/main/input/sunset_boulevard_walk.png)\n\nMake one continuous shot longer than a single H3 sampling window. `MiniMax H3 Context Windows` cuts the latent into overlapping windows, samples each one, then fuses them back. The 10 s default runs as **3 windows of 124 frames, 39 frames of overlap**.\n\n1. **Duration** - seconds; the expression snaps it to H3's 17k+5 frame grid at 24 fps (10 s -> 243 frames).\n2. **Context Windows** - `context_length` / `context_overlap` must be 17n+5; windows start on H3's 17-frame chunks so picture and audio stay in sync.\n3. **Sampler** - `fuse_method` pyramid blends the seams, `freenoise` shuffles window noise.\n\nLonger windows = fewer seams but more VRAM per window. One window is trained for 124-362 frames; context windows push past that."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## MiniMax H3: Long Video (Context Windows)\n\n**Input Assets**\n- [sunset_boulevard_walk.png](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Comfy-Org/workflow_templates/refs/heads/main/input/sunset_boulevard_walk.png)\n\nMake one continuous shot longer than a single H3 sampling window. `MiniMax H3 Context Windows` cuts the latent into overlapping windows, samples each one, then fuses them back. The 10 s default runs as **3 windows of 124 frames, 39 frames of overlap**.\n\n1. **Duration** - seconds; the expression snaps it to H3's 17k+5 frame grid at 24 fps (10 s -> 243 frames).\n2. **Context Windows** - `context_length` / `context_overlap` must be 17n+5; windows start on H3's 17-frame chunks so picture and audio stay in sync.\n3. **Sampler** - `fuse_method` pyramid blends the seams, `freenoise` shuffles window noise.\n\nLonger windows = fewer seams but more VRAM per window. One window is trained for 124-362 frames; context windows push past that."
      }
    },
